From dd7f82ceb6e24458ef7acb9ef5d66f3485d9dee6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:58:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: MSE playback with one GStreamer stream per
 SourceBuffer

YouTube appends audio and video to separate SourceBuffers, each with its
own initialization segment. Pushing both into one byte stream made a
single matroskademux see two incompatible headers, so video stayed black.
ServoMseSrc exposes one appsrc per SourceBuffer as a sometimes-pad, so
urisourcebin demuxes each stream on its own. SourceBuffer.buffered now
comes from parsing WebM and fMP4 segment timestamps.

update_media_state paused a playing element on every state update; it now
pauses only when the element stops being potentially playing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
